# Cortex AI — Production Dependencies (Abstract Spec)
# =====================================================
# This file is the HUMAN-EDITED source of truth.
# Do NOT edit requirements.lock directly — it is machine-generated.
#
# Workflow:
#   Edit this file → run `make lock` → commit both files → deploy from .lock
#
# Upgrade policy (see docs/dependency-management.md):
#   Any change to the ML stack (numpy, pandas, torch, tensorflow, scikit-learn,
#   xgboost, onnx) must be accompanied by a backtest diff and explicit sign-off.
#   Run `make audit` after every dependency change.

# ── Non-PyPI index for PyTorch CPU wheels ─────────────────────────────────────
# torch is the ONLY package sourced from this index.  All other packages resolve
# from PyPI.  The CPU wheel is required because the RTX 3050 (4 GB VRAM) on this
# host is allocated exclusively to TensorFlow; torch uses CPU-only inference.
--extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu

